Accept the full scale range of the background image

The image loader took a scale from 17 to 1023 pixels on each axis. The
configuration dialog offers 16 to 1024 on its two spin boxes. A saved
width or height of 16 or 1024 therefore left the background image
unloaded. The window kept the plain colour and gave no message.

Make the two bounds of the loader inclusive. The loader then takes every
value that the dialog can write.

The change sits on the branch work/image-dialog of the local tree, as commit 1 of 5.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

diff --git a/qt6/common/config_file.cpp b/qt6/common/config_file.cpp
index bfd40ec3..813b3b4b 100644
--- a/qt6/common/config_file.cpp
+++ b/qt6/common/config_file.cpp
@@ -595,8 +595,11 @@ void qtcSetBarHidden(const QString &app, bool hidden, const char *prefix)
 
 void qtcLoadBgndImage(QtCImage *img)
 {
+    // The two bounds are pixels. MIN_SIZE and MAX_SIZE of
+    // qt6/config/imagepropertiesdialog.cpp hold the same pair for the two
+    // scale spin boxes.
     if(!img->loaded &&
-        ( (img->width>16 && img->width<1024 && img->height>16 && img->height<1024) || (0==img->width && 0==img->height)) )
+        ( (img->width>=16 && img->width<=1024 && img->height>=16 && img->height<=1024) || (0==img->width && 0==img->height)) )
     {
         img->loaded=true;
         img->pixmap.img=QPixmap();
